Dialogue: 3,0:02:34.38,0:02:40.13,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PLAN · REED, VAUGHAN & SHAKESPEARE, TYPHOID FEVER REPORT (1904)
Dialogue: 3,0:02:34.38,0:02:40.13,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ROUGH PLOT OF THE 201ST NEW YORK AT CAMP BLACK · JULY 26 TO SEPT. 9, 1898
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.60,0:03:04.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}What Reed saw was not mysterious.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.55,0:03:07.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In accounts of his visit, the latrines were filled
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.50,0:03:10.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to the top, and flies moved between them and the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.34,0:03:10.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}men's food.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:02.85,0:03:08.60,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1810 0 l 1810 132 l 0 132{\p0}
