Dialogue: 3,0:03:02.85,0:03:08.60,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PLAN · REED, VAUGHAN & SHAKESPEARE, TYPHOID FEVER REPORT (1904)
Dialogue: 3,0:03:02.85,0:03:08.60,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}2ND NEW JERSEY · PLAN OF CAMP, TYPHOID CASES AMONG THE TENTS · JACKSONVILLE, 1898
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.43,0:03:14.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Board's report describes flies as one way the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.47,0:03:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}disease spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.40,0:03:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Decades later, the Army was still teaching the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.25,0:03:21.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}lesson about flies, in a training cartoon about
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.16,0:03:24.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}dysentery, with flies crawling over a mess kit.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:11.68,0:03:17.43,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 676 0 l 676 132 l 0 132{\p0}
