Dialogue: 3,0:11:34.49,0:11:40.24,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE ELEVENTH 'U.S.' · CAMP AT ALEXANDRIA, VA., 1861
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.13,0:12:42.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Why two to one, and not one and a half?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.30,0:12:45.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The two counts come from different tables, and they
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.14,0:12:47.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}do not define their categories in the same way.
Dialogue: 2,0:12:40.38,0:12:46.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1210 0 l 1210 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:40.38,0:12:46.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:40.38,0:12:46.13,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:12:40.38,0:12:46.13,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIRST MINNESOTA INFANTRY · CAMP STONE, MD., JAN. 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.98,0:12:58.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Either way, the direction does not change.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.23,0:13:00.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For the Union army, the camp was deadlier than the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.91,0:13:01.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}battlefield.
Dialogue: 2,0:12:56.23,0:13:01.95,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1146 0 l 1146 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:56.23,0:13:01.95,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:12:56.23,0:13:01.95,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:12:56.23,0:13:01.95,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"RUSHING UP A CAMP" · A UNION CAMP, VIRGINIA, 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.56,0:13:23.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Dysentery alone made up one quarter of all reported
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.80,0:13:24.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}sicknesses.
Dialogue: 2,0:13:20.81,0:13:24.90,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1617 0 l 1617 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:20.81,0:13:24.90,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:20.81,0:13:24.90,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:13:20.81,0:13:24.90,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}COOKING, WASHING AND POLISHING IN A UNION CAMP · YORKTOWN, VA., MAY 1862
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.06,0:13:54.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Typhoid, 34,833 deaths in that table.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.65,0:13:59.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The National Museum of Civil War Medicine gives a
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.39,0:14:01.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}lower count, about 27,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.90,0:14:03.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Sources disagree.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.55,0:14:05.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every version is grim.
Dialogue: 2,0:13:51.31,0:13:57.06,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1381 0 l 1381 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:51.31,0:13:57.06,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:13:51.31,0:13:57.06,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:13:51.31,0:13:57.06,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A COVERED WELL, GUARDED TO PREVENT WASTE · VIRGINIA, MAY 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.13,0:14:09.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Malaria, 10,063 deaths. Typhus, 958.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.36,0:14:13.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And pneumonia, the museum says, killed 20,000 Union
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.94,0:14:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}troops.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:06.38,0:14:12.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1031 0 l 1031 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:06.38,0:14:12.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:06.38,0:14:12.13,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:14:06.38,0:14:12.13,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A BATH IN THE NORTH ANNA RIVER · MAY 1864
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.12,0:14:33.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was the sum.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.04,0:14:35.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Add only those four lines, and you pass 90,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.92,0:14:38.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then add everything else a camp could do to a man.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:32.37,0:14:38.12,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1360 0 l 1360 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:32.37,0:14:38.12,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:32.37,0:14:38.12,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · PHOTOGRAPHIC HISTORY OF THE CIVIL WAR, VOL. 8 (1911)
Dialogue: 3,0:14:32.37,0:14:38.12,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE 114TH PENNSYLVANIA · BRANDY STATION, VA., WINTER OF 1863
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.39,0:15:01.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A latrine in the wrong place could foul the water a
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.42,0:15:02.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}camp depended on.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.43,0:15:05.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Water came from wells and rivers, and the army drank
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.52,0:15:06.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}what it found.
Dialogue: 2,0:14:58.64,0:15:04.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1424 0 l 1424 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:14:58.64,0:15:04.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
