Dialogue: 3,0:27:05.56,0:27:11.31,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}LINE SERVICE, MESS HALL · CAMP MEADE, MARYLAND · 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.39,0:27:21.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From the S.S.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.41,0:27:25.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Grant, a sailor on another ship counted 15 burials
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.35,0:27:27.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}at sea in a single day.
Dialogue: 2,0:27:20.64,0:27:26.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 870 0 l 870 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:20.64,0:27:26.39,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:27:20.64,0:27:26.39,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS FILM · 83RD DIVISION · NARA
Dialogue: 3,0:27:20.64,0:27:26.39,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}CAMP SHERMAN, OHIO · 1917–18
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.09,0:28:29.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The flu reached cities too.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.12,0:28:32.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This is a parade in San Francisco in 1918,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.27,0:28:34.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}celebrating the end of the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.60,0:28:38.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The archive says the paraders are all wearing flu masks.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:27.34,0:28:33.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1446 0 l 1446 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:27.34,0:28:33.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:27.34,0:28:33.09,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PARADERS IN GAUZE MASKS · NEWSREEL FILM · PRELINGER ARCHIVES (ARCHIVE'S DESCRIPTION)
Dialogue: 3,0:28:27.34,0:28:33.09,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SAN FRANCISCO · PARADE CELEBRATING THE END OF WORLD WAR I · 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.26,0:28:41.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So how many soldiers died of influenza?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.75,0:28:43.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The sources do not agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.35,0:28:44.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}We will show you each one.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:39.51,0:28:45.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1446 0 l 1446 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:39.51,0:28:45.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:39.51,0:28:45.26,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PARADERS IN GAUZE MASKS · NEWSREEL FILM · PRELINGER ARCHIVES (ARCHIVE'S DESCRIPTION)
Dialogue: 3,0:28:39.51,0:28:45.26,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SAN FRANCISCO · PARADE CELEBRATING THE END OF WORLD WAR I · 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.58,0:28:59.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Navy's history says more than 44,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.14,0:29:03.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the University of Kansas Medical Center cites
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.40,0:29:07.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}24,664, adding that most of those deaths came from
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.75,0:29:10.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}complicating bacterial pneumonia.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:55.83,0:29:01.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1192 0 l 1192 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:55.83,0:29:01.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:55.83,0:29:01.58,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. OF THE U.S. ARMY IN THE WORLD WAR, VOL. 6 (1926)
Dialogue: 3,0:28:55.83,0:29:01.58,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}OLD CAMP AT GRANGE NEUVE · GIRONDE, FRANCE · 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.07,0:29:13.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That is why we lean on the World War numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.77,0:29:16.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Congressional Research Service warns that
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.48,0:29:19.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}casualty records before it are often incomplete.
Dialogue: 2,0:29:11.32,0:29:17.07,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1296 0 l 1296 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.32,0:29:17.07,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.32,0:29:17.07,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARMY MEDICAL DEPARTMENT IN THE WORLD WAR, VOL. 6 (SANITATION)
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.32,0:29:17.07,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}KITCHEN OF COMPANY A, 126TH INFANTRY, 32D DIVISION · 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.15,0:30:10.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For the World War, non-battle deaths outnumbered
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.11,0:30:13.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}battle deaths in the Army, and influenza was a large
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.32,0:30:13.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}part of it.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:07.40,0:30:13.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 870 0 l 870 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.40,0:30:13.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.40,0:30:13.15,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS FILM · 83RD DIVISION · NARA
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.40,0:30:13.15,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}CAMP SHERMAN, OHIO · 1917–18
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.45,0:30:17.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Twenty years later, in the next world war, the
Dialogue: 0,0:30:17.32,0:30:18.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}pattern broke.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.20,0:30:20.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Disease still filled the hospitals.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.38,0:30:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But it no longer killed more soldiers than bullets.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:14.70,0:30:20.45,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 870 0 l 870 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:14.70,0:30:20.45,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:14.70,0:30:20.45,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS FILM · 83RD DIVISION · NARA
Dialogue: 3,0:30:14.70,0:30:20.45,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}CAMP SHERMAN, OHIO · 1917–18
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.83,0:30:55.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But there is more than one way to count a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.53,0:30:58.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Count the medical admissions, and the picture turns
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.52,0:30:59.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}upside down.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:53.08,0:30:58.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1482 0 l 1482 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:53.08,0:30:58.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:53.08,0:30:58.83,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY FILM BULLETIN 147 · MEDICAL SERVICE IN THE JUNGLE · 1944 · LOCATION NOT STATED
Dialogue: 3,0:30:53.08,0:30:58.83,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}APPROACH FROM THE SEA
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.69,0:31:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Disease did not win the count of the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.89,0:31:22.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It won the count of the sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.41,0:31:24.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And in the South Pacific, the name that came up
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.87,0:31:26.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}again and again was malaria.
Dialogue: 2,0:31:18.94,0:31:24.69,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1482 0 l 1482 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:18.94,0:31:24.69,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:18.94,0:31:24.69,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY FILM BULLETIN 147 · MEDICAL SERVICE IN THE JUNGLE · 1944 · LOCATION NOT STATED
Dialogue: 3,0:31:18.94,0:31:24.69,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}JUNGLE SHORELINE
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.23,0:33:19.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So the Army built an answer, and it was mostly people.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.51,0:33:22.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Survey units found where the mosquitoes bred.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.24,0:33:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Control units drained, cleared, and oiled.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.79,0:33:27.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They trained at places like the Army School of
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.59,0:33:29.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Malariology, in the Panama Canal Zone.
Dialogue: 2,0:33:16.48,0:33:22.23,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1360 0 l 1360 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:16.48,0:33:22.23,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:16.48,0:33:22.23,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARMY, PREVENTIVE MEDICINE IN WORLD WAR II, VOL. VI (1963)
Dialogue: 3,0:33:16.48,0:33:22.23,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARMY SCHOOL OF MALARIOLOGY · FORT CLAYTON, CANAL ZONE · 1943
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.56,0:33:45.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Drainage was the simplest weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.44,0:33:48.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Take away the standing water, and you take away the
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.33,0:33:48.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}nursery.
Dialogue: 2,0:33:43.81,0:33:49.19,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1467 0 l 1467 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:43.81,0:33:49.19,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:43.81,0:33:49.19,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARMY, PREVENTIVE MEDICINE IN WORLD WAR II, VOL. VI (1963)
Dialogue: 3,0:33:43.81,0:33:49.19,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A MALARIA CONTROL UNIT LEARNS DRAINAGE · CAMP PLAUCHE, LA. · 1943
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.24,0:33:52.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A Navy film from the time shows the work.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.08,0:33:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A laboratory bench. A microscope.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.37,0:33:55.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Larvae in a jar.
Dialogue: 2,0:33:49.49,0:33:55.24,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1788 0 l 1788 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:49.49,0:33:55.24,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:49.49,0:33:55.24,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. NAVY FILM · MALARIA AND MOSQUITO CONTROL ACTIVITIES (MUNDA, NEW GEORGIA, AND LICATA, SICILY) · 1943–44
Dialogue: 3,0:33:49.49,0:33:55.24,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}MALARIA CONTROL LABORATORY WORK
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.93,0:33:58.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And inspectors in the field, dipping larvae out of
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.79,0:34:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}puddles and drainage ditches.
Dialogue: 2,0:33:56.18,0:34:00.85,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1788 0 l 1788 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:56.18,0:34:00.85,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:33:56.18,0:34:00.85,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. NAVY FILM · MALARIA AND MOSQUITO CONTROL ACTIVITIES (MUNDA, NEW GEORGIA, AND LICATA, SICILY) · 1943–44
Dialogue: 3,0:33:56.18,0:34:00.85,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}INSPECTORS CHECKING STANDING WATER
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.90,0:34:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then came DDT.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.97,0:34:05.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Army's malaria history says the first field
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.55,0:34:09.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}trial of a DDT residual spray took place in Italy,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.35,0:34:09.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}in 1944.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.96,0:34:13.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The same history shows it being applied by hand in
